            <ArticleTitle>[Headache caused by distortion of the nasal septum and respiratory disturbances of the nasal cavity].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>467-74</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Head and facial pain of unknown origin may be caused by defective aeration of nose and sinus. The reason is a chronic irritation of the mucosa or direct contact between septum and conchal mucosa. A secondary reaction to the impaired breathing through the nose may be an irritation of the sinus without causing a full-grown sinusitis. Diagnosis and therapy are possible by rhinoscopy, sinumanometry and sinuscopy in one appointment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
